= Blood pressure — Simple =

'''Blood pressure''' describes how strongly blood pushes against artery walls as the heart pumps.

A typical measurement has two numbers. The first is the higher pressure while the heart pumps (systolic). The second is the lower pressure between beats (diastolic). They are usually written together, such as 120/80.

A blood-pressure reading is not the same as a [[Pulse|pulse]] rate. Both can change with activity or other conditions. Doctors use correctly taken measurements, usually more than one, with the person's health context.

